  {"comment": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT. GitHub #582's design (mitcad#2272; opened with --open, never committed; tools/cli/fillet-nozzle-dome-reported-test.cmake; the design as fillet_nozzle_dome_reported.json describes it)."},
  {"comment": "Fillet2 taken out, and the original nozzle's foot (picked by its dome edge) added to Fillet1 (F17), which rounds the flange's foot with 1.5 before the pattern, as the reporter tried first: Fillet1 builds at the exact size without a note, and the pattern repeats it on the copies' feet. Before, Fillet1 failed as the original's foot does after the pattern."},
  {"comment": "The public benchmark this design follows ends with a fillet and a chamfer (its step 9) and a circular pattern of them (step 10, mitcad#2372): here Chamfer2 (F16, 1 mm on the flange's outer edge at its underside) and Fillet1 (F17), both among CircularPattern2's (F18) features, four elements about z. The pattern repeats both on its three copies; their faces are the pattern's (F18:fillet(...), F18:chamfer(...) on the copies' edges). Each copy's foot is checked by its sharp edges being gone, since a copy's foot edge on the dome can lie in two pieces whose rounding faces carry the piece's number."},
  {"cmd": "delete_feature", "uid": "F19"},
  {"cmd": "edit_feature", "uid": "F17", "def": {"type": "fillet", "body": "F2.b0", "edges": ["E{F5:side(c1)|F7:start(r{c1})}", "E{F2:side(c17[c2+c3,c19])|F5:side(c1)}"], "radius": 1.5}},
